# Line endings.
#
# The project is written on Windows and runs on Linux. Without this file a
# shell script committed from Windows arrives with CRLF, and the kernel
# refuses it with "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M" — an error that says
# nothing about its real cause.
#
# So everything that Linux executes or reads as configuration is stored and
# checked out with LF, whatever the machine it was edited on.
* text=auto

*.sh        text eol=lf
*.service   text eol=lf
*.timer     text eol=lf
*.conf      text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
